Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.45,0:00:12.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,
Dialogue: 99,0:00:24.34,0:00:29.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For counter-terrorism, the most efficient tactic is not simply reinforcing the military or police.
Dialogue: 99,0:00:29.69,0:00:34.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Instead, the most effective \Nresponse to their tactics...
Dialogue: 99,0:00:34.54,0:00:37.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,, is to have experienced specialists \Nswiftly apprehend them.
Dialogue: 99,0:00:41.52,0:00:48.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Above all, the best counter-terrorism measures prevent terrorism before it even happens.
Dialogue: 99,0:01:13.85,0:01:18.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On top of that, they'd also be in charge of uncovering and breaking up organized terrorism.
Dialogue: 99,0:01:18.85,0:01:23.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But in reality, \Nfew groups can do all of this.
Dialogue: 99,0:01:50.67,0:01:53.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are some specialist \Ncounter-terrorist groups.
Dialogue: 99,0:01:53.89,0:01:59.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,G9 in Germany, SAS in Britain, \Nand the American Special Commandos.
Dialogue: 99,0:01:59.43,0:02:05.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But they're tightly controlled\N and can only be dispatched domestically.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:06.97,0:02:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Terrorists may have no borders,\N but we have political borders to contend with.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:14.78,0:02:15.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However!
Dialogue: 99,0:02:16.28,0:02:21.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is only one counter-terrorism group not restricted by political borders.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:21.91,0:02:24.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are called "CAT," \Na civilian organization.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:24.12,0:02:29.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Upon request, they can have counter-terrorist\N specialists dispatched to any part of the world.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:30.59,0:02:32.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're almost done.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:32.30,0:02:33.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were our casualties?
Dialogue: 99,0:02:33.47,0:02:36.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elly and Shirley from \Nthe First Squad were hurt.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:36.09,0:02:39.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the Second Squad,\N only Nina was injured.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:39.56,0:02:41.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about the terrorists?
Dialogue: 99,0:02:41.47,0:02:43.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eight were injured, \Nsix were killed.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:45.06,0:02:46.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's Jessica?
Dialogue: 99,0:02:46.90,0:02:49.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She must still be disarming it.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:49.77,0:02:52.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our dear "Mother"\N is probably singing a lullaby.
Dialogue: 99,0:02:53.44,0:02:56.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go to sleep, good baby...
Dialogue: 99,0:02:56.91,0:03:00.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When a baby is about to fall asleep,\N even the slightest noise will wake them up.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:01.54,0:03:03.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if this one starts crying, \Nwe'll be in big trouble.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:03.83,0:03:04.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What'll happen?
Dialogue: 99,0:03:04.87,0:03:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You and I both will be \Npaying God a little visit.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:21.14,0:03:23.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Time for the finishing touch.\N I'm cutting the red wire.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:24.27,0:03:26.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're scared, fall back\N with the captain and the others.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:29.11,0:03:31.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The red wire trips the cutoff.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:31.36,0:03:35.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So if you cut the white and blue wires, \Nyou can cut it without jamming it.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:35.86,0:03:38.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's connected to the timer.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:38.87,0:03:43.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People think that the timer just lets \Nthe electricity flow when time's up.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:44.75,0:03:49.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you can make it cut the flow of electricity when time's up, too.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:52.00,0:03:55.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the count of three, \Nhit the converter switch.
Dialogue: 99,0:03:55.80,0:04:00.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mess up, we're history. Your boyfriend \Nwill be told you died in the line of duty.
Dialogue: 99,0:04:15.82,0:04:17.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ready? I'm cutting it.
Dialogue: 99,0:04:31.25,0:04:32.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One...
Dialogue: 99,0:04:32.21,0:04:33.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Two...
Dialogue: 99,0:04:33.38,0:04:34.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Three!
Dialogue: 99,0:04:54.15,0:04:56.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's still fast asleep.
Dialogue: 99,0:04:56.07,0:04:57.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now we're in the clear.
Dialogue: 99,0:04:59.65,0:05:00.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is he asleep?
Dialogue: 99,0:05:00.53,0:05:02.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yep. Nice and quiet, \Nlike a good boy.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:04.41,0:05:07.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Helga, check personnel \Nand equipment.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:07.67,0:05:08.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aye, ma'am!
Dialogue: 99,0:05:09.41,0:05:13.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's withdraw.\NOperation completed, 12:00.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:13.05,0:05:14.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move out!
Dialogue: 99,0:05:21.68,0:05:27.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That video was taken three weeks ago, two days before the International Conference in Cologne.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:27.31,0:05:32.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,CAT raided the hideout of a terrorist group called "The Silver Calvary."
Dialogue: 99,0:05:32.40,0:05:37.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They confiscated guns and explosives that were going to be used in an attack on the convention.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:38.11,0:05:43.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were mostly women in that clip.\N What are they, assistants?
Dialogue: 99,0:05:43.61,0:05:45.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those women carried \Nout the operation.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:46.19,0:05:47.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 99,0:05:48.41,0:05:50.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hand out the datasheets.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:50.00,0:05:50.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 99,0:05:56.92,0:05:58.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:00.01,0:06:03.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her real name is Mariko Rosebank.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:03.13,0:06:04.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Twenty-six years old.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:07.01,0:06:08.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An Asian woman?
Dialogue: 99,0:06:08.35,0:06:10.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By her name, I assume she's second-generation Japanese?
Dialogue: 99,0:06:10.81,0:06:12.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, she sure is easy on the eyes, huh?
Dialogue: 99,0:06:12.81,0:06:15.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's got quite a figure,\N and her black hair suits her, too.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:17.69,0:06:21.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's one of the few \Nfemale commanders in CAT.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:21.44,0:06:25.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her operations succeed an amazing ninety percent of the time.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:25.49,0:06:27.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because she only takes easy jobs, right?
Dialogue: 99,0:06:27.87,0:06:30.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know, jobs without \Nany high risks.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:30.91,0:06:35.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's seen combat in places like Angola, Southwest Africa,
Dialogue: 99,0:06:35.54,0:06:39.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bolivia, Nicaragua, Bangladesh, and Iran in the past three years.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:39.09,0:06:43.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These areas are some of the world's biggest powder kegs.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:43.22,0:06:48.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Out of respect, many soldiers who have done operations with her call her "Rose Mary."
Dialogue: 99,0:06:51.27,0:06:52.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose Mary?
Dialogue: 99,0:06:52.68,0:06:55.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a name only the roughest \Nmercenaries could come up with.
Dialogue: 99,0:06:55.60,0:06:59.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It probably comes from \Nher surname, "Rosebank."
Dialogue: 99,0:07:01.15,0:07:02.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does it matter?!
Dialogue: 99,0:07:02.44,0:07:08.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So what if she has combat experience, \Na romantic name, and unmatched beauty?
Dialogue: 99,0:07:08.45,0:07:12.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need a dime-novel\N heroine or a fashion model!
Dialogue: 99,0:07:12.91,0:07:19.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. We need assurance that our \NVIPs will be protected from the terrorists.
Dialogue: 99,0:07:20.13,0:07:22.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I am aware.
Dialogue: 99,0:07:22.59,0:07:24.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you guarantee such a thing?
Dialogue: 99,0:07:24.63,0:07:28.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're the best of the best.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:18.52,0:08:22.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a stylish new shop just \Naround the corner on 2nd Avenue.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:22.48,0:08:23.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wanna go?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:23.94,0:08:25.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Time flies, huh?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:25.36,0:08:28.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was under construction when \Nwe left for our last operation, right?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:28.53,0:08:32.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Della said they carry \Na lot of designer brands.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:33.20,0:08:35.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, she already scoped it out?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:35.16,0:08:39.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll be going to Florida after \Nthe intensive training camp next week, right?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:39.17,0:08:41.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to look at the swimsuits.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:42.21,0:08:44.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have a target?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:44.17,0:08:45.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:45.34,0:08:46.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just need to carry it out.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:46.92,0:08:48.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's our mission objective?
Dialogue: 99,0:08:49.51,0:08:51.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Bag a bargain!\N - Bag a bargain!
Dialogue: 99,0:08:53.01,0:08:57.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Captain Rosebank from Division M, \Nplease report to headquarters immediately.
Dialogue: 99,0:08:57.18,0:09:00.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Repeat, Captain Rosebank from Division M, please report to—
Dialogue: 99,0:09:04.73,0:09:05.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not a bad haul.
Dialogue: 99,0:09:05.40,0:09:07.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Easy as that.\N- Wow!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:10.70,0:09:12.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I bagged a bargain.
Dialogue: 99,0:09:12.20,0:09:14.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Florida men...
Dialogue: 99,0:09:14.33,0:09:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a filthy mind.
Dialogue: 99,0:09:15.70,0:09:18.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I bet you're thinking about \Nsomething pervy, Irene!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:18.20,0:09:19.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brats like you should be quiet.
Dialogue: 99,0:09:19.66,0:09:23.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you weren't wearing a bikini, they'd never know where your boobs end and your torso begins!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:24.63,0:09:25.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's so mean!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:25.75,0:09:26.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate you, Irene!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:26.75,0:09:27.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Flat-chested!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:27.35,0:09:29.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- So what if you have big boobs?! \N- You're such a child!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:29.09,0:09:31.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- You're so, so, so mean! \N- But it's true, you know?!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:31.51,0:09:32.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop it! Both of you!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:33.26,0:09:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't make such \Na fuss in Florida, okay?
Dialogue: 99,0:09:36.22,0:09:38.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to enjoy a quiet vacation.
Dialogue: 99,0:09:44.61,0:09:45.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What?
Dialogue: 99,0:09:45.98,0:09:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A-A quiet vacation... wearing that?
Dialogue: 99,0:09:48.34,0:09:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That thing's got a pretty \Nloud design, you kn—
Dialogue: 99,0:09:50.24,0:09:51.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:51.40,0:09:55.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's none of your business \Nhow I enjoy my vacation!
Dialogue: 99,0:09:55.83,0:09:57.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's quite the bargain.
Dialogue: 99,0:09:57.20,0:09:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do they accept returns?
Dialogue: 99,0:09:59.04,0:10:00.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, what are you...
Dialogue: 99,0:10:00.70,0:10:02.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going north.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:02.79,0:10:05.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No more intensive training camp.\NNo vacation in Florida, either.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:05.46,0:10:06.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 99,0:10:06.67,0:10:11.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The operation will be in Switzerland.\NYou'll need sweaters, and Equipment B and C.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:11.01,0:10:14.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Depending on how things go, \Nwe might need Container E as well.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:15.14,0:10:16.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We leave tonight.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:27.19,0:10:31.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The unification of East and West Germany is going about as well as you would expect.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:31.28,0:10:36.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their economic differences are too great.\NJust destroying the Wall wasn't going to solve it.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:38.20,0:10:42.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If discontent continues to grow, the people will need a way to relieve the stress.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:42.54,0:10:47.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if the needs of the citizens don't match the schedule of the politicians...
Dialogue: 99,0:10:47.04,0:10:49.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's when terrorism happens, right?
Dialogue: 99,0:10:49.25,0:10:53.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, are we planning the operation in Switzerland and carrying it out in Germany?
Dialogue: 99,0:10:53.17,0:10:55.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No. The operation will \Ntake place in Switzerland, too.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:55.97,0:10:59.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's going to be an unofficial \Nconference between the East and the West.
Dialogue: 99,0:10:59.56,0:11:04.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not just East and West Germany, \Nbut the East and West as a whole?
Dialogue: 99,0:11:04.89,0:11:07.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right. The president of America,
Dialogue: 99,0:11:07.65,0:11:11.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the leader of Perestroika, \Nand the Iron Woman's successor.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:12.44,0:11:20.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A terrorist with a nuclear missile could change \Nthe world in fifteen minutes and two seconds.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:22.91,0:11:26.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there aren't any terrorists with \Nenough money to buy a nuclear warhead.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:27.88,0:11:30.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,More than likely, \Nthey'll set a time bomb.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:30.71,0:11:35.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, these terrorists hold \Nthe key to the apocalypse itself.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:36.18,0:11:37.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama!
Dialogue: 99,0:11:37.30,0:11:38.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, there's a plane!
Dialogue: 99,0:11:38.93,0:11:41.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Timmy, you'll fall \Nif you run like that.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:49.19,0:11:52.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, who was crying \Nwhen they skinned their knee?
Dialogue: 99,0:11:52.69,0:11:55.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, my, he knows all \Nthe tricks to get your attention now.
Dialogue: 99,0:11:55.78,0:11:57.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You do the same, \Ndon't you, Daddy?
Dialogue: 99,0:12:04.12,0:12:06.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to London for \Na week on a business trip.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:06.46,0:12:08.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be back before you know it.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:08.04,0:12:09.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know you will.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:10.00,0:12:14.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But this is the first time since we married \Nthat we'll be apart for more than three days.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:14.30,0:12:15.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course I'm worried...
Dialogue: 99,0:12:33.40,0:12:34.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Timmy!
Dialogue: 99,0:12:34.94,0:12:36.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mr. Timothy Rosebank!
Dialogue: 99,0:12:37.28,0:12:43.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Will you promise to protect Mrs. Mary \NRosebank while I'm gone this week?
Dialogue: 99,0:12:44.70,0:12:46.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I promise, Papa.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:46.33,0:12:48.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay. Good boy.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:50.62,0:12:52.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you want for a souvenir?
Dialogue: 99,0:12:52.00,0:12:55.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Queen Elizabeth's crown, \Nor the Imperial Guards from Buckingham?
Dialogue: 99,0:12:56.09,0:12:59.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Queen will get in \Ntrouble if her crown is missing.
Dialogue: 99,0:12:59.34,0:13:02.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I don't want Mama to have \Nto cook for all the Imperial Guards.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:02.89,0:13:05.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, bring me back a teddy bear!
Dialogue: 99,0:13:05.14,0:13:06.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A really big one.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:06.81,0:13:08.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, got it.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:08.39,0:13:09.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look forward to it.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:13.61,0:13:16.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think your mama wants \Na big teddy bear, too.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:19.32,0:13:20.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, would you look at the time?
Dialogue: 99,0:13:21.28,0:13:25.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I need to go meet \Nmy business partner inside the gate.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:25.20,0:13:26.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll have to say goodbye here.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:28.58,0:13:30.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once I'm gone, \Ngo straight home.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:30.83,0:13:32.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't take any detours.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:32.96,0:13:36.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure, we'll go straight home.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:36.84,0:13:39.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But looking around \Nthe airport isn't a detour.
Dialogue: 99,0:13:39.30,0:13:41.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama, you're so smart!
Dialogue: 99,0:13:53.98,0:13:56.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama, just a little bit higher!
Dialogue: 99,0:13:58.90,0:14:00.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We did it!
Dialogue: 99,0:14:03.16,0:14:10.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}This is the final call for passengers traveling to \NLondon via Florida on British Airways Flight #122.
Dialogue: 99,0:14:10.45,0:14:14.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Will the passengers of British Airways Flight #122 please...
Dialogue: 99,0:14:10.79,0:14:12.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the plane Papa's on! \NRight, Mama?
Dialogue: 99,0:14:12.92,0:14:13.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Timmy!
Dialogue: 99,0:14:13.36,0:14:14.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can see the gate from here!
Dialogue: 99,0:14:14.90,0:14:17.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Maybe I'll see Papa boarding it!\N - Timmy.
Dialogue: 99,0:14:24.13,0:14:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Timmy, come here.
Dialogue: 99,0:14:26.43,0:14:29.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't tell which one is Papa's.
Dialogue: 99,0:14:53.12,0:14:55.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Help us!\N- Someone help!
Dialogue: 99,0:15:05.26,0:15:07.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,T-Timmy...
Dialogue: 99,0:15:19.90,0:15:23.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Should I turn up the air conditioner? You're soaked in sweat.
Dialogue: 99,0:15:25.28,0:15:27.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was it the rose dream again?
Dialogue: 99,0:15:27.49,0:15:31.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. Whenever I get nervous, \NI have the same dream.
Dialogue: 99,0:15:33.58,0:15:35.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My husband, my boy...
Dialogue: 99,0:15:36.29,0:15:38.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They took everything \Naway from me.
Dialogue: 99,0:15:38.29,0:15:40.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate terrorists.
Dialogue: 99,0:15:40.75,0:15:41.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary...
Dialogue: 99,0:15:43.30,0:15:45.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They left me here, to survive...
Dialogue: 99,0:15:45.30,0:15:47.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate terrorists.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:01.77,0:16:06.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx95}Here's the site of the operation. In other words, \Nthis is where the East-West summit will take place.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:06.40,0:16:09.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Interlaken?!\N That's pretty remote!
Dialogue: 99,0:16:09.91,0:16:11.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it that remote?
Dialogue: 99,0:16:11.66,0:16:13.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not that remote.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:13.66,0:16:17.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People who climb the Alps have \Nused it as a base for a long time now.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:17.00,0:16:20.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The north face of the Eiger, the Jungfraujoch, the Matterhorn...
Dialogue: 99,0:16:20.50,0:16:22.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a mountain climber's Mecca.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:23.55,0:16:27.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The site of the summit is thirty minutes away from Interlaken by car.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:27.47,0:16:29.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be at the Bachhelner mountain villa.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:29.93,0:16:33.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Should we assume that information\N has already leaked to the terrorists?
Dialogue: 99,0:16:33.68,0:16:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'd better be prepared, \Nin case it has.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:36.33,0:16:37.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The summit will be two days long.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:37.77,0:16:42.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because of its unofficial nature,\N each VIP is bringing minimal staff with them.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:42.61,0:16:45.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Except for the VIPs, only women \Nmay enter the summit building.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:48.50,0:16:52.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, we're gonna be hostesses\N and special guards?
Dialogue: 99,0:16:52.70,0:16:53.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 99,0:16:53.95,0:16:58.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, they think women can't be terrorists? \NKind of a bold assumption, huh?
Dialogue: 99,0:16:58.37,0:17:04.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Given that most members of terrorist \Ngroups are men, it's a reasonable one.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:04.59,0:17:08.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm amazed that the Secret Service \Nand SAS approved the idea.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:08.13,0:17:13.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what about the security for the summit site,\N or around the villa during the summit?
Dialogue: 99,0:17:13.58,0:17:17.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Swiss Army and Swiss Mountain Police will take care of security.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:18.41,0:17:22.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All the VIPs will be transported from the airport to the villa tomorrow via helicopters.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:22.56,0:17:25.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They'll stay the night \Nat the villa as well.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:25.36,0:17:27.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, a confined conference?
Dialogue: 99,0:17:28.18,0:17:32.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, are we accompanying \Nthem at night—
Dialogue: 99,0:17:33.32,0:17:35.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're not call girls!
Dialogue: 99,0:17:35.66,0:17:38.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, y'know, we'd be able\N to guard them very closely.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:39.91,0:17:44.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, free love is fine by me, \Nso that's not a bad plan.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:44.25,0:17:47.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But don't forget,\N their wives will be with them.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:47.35,0:17:51.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-That's unfair! You said we were gonna be the only girls there!
Dialogue: 99,0:17:51.09,0:17:52.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Irene!
Dialogue: 99,0:17:52.26,0:17:54.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, I'd rather not cause \Nan international scandal.
Dialogue: 99,0:17:54.59,0:17:55.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:17:55.93,0:17:59.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are we checking the interior and \Nsurroundings of the conference building?
Dialogue: 99,0:17:59.52,0:18:03.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Swiss government has already checked the building and 2 km around it.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:03.85,0:18:07.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They chose the conference \Nsite just a week ago,
Dialogue: 99,0:18:07.11,0:18:10.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so it's unlikely there's \Na bomb inside the building.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:18.20,0:18:23.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Swiss Army, 12th Division, 1st Squadron,\N Lieutenant Colonel Ernst Heineken.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:24.12,0:18:26.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Welcome, ladies from CAT.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:26.96,0:18:31.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the CAT Overseas Tactical \NHead Officer, Rosebank.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:31.55,0:18:33.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pleased to meet you, \NLt. Col. Heineken.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:33.43,0:18:36.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The pleasure is mine, to be in \Nthe company of such beautiful ladies.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:36.41,0:18:39.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Wow, look at that! \N- How romantic.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:39.06,0:18:39.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a player.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:39.64,0:18:42.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,European military guys \Nsure are cool.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:42.64,0:18:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the Swiss Mountain Units, their elite \Nforces wear those Edelweiss emblems.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:47.65,0:18:49.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean they're \Nspecial commandos?
Dialogue: 99,0:18:49.32,0:18:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are, but because they're part of the Swiss\N forces they have to remain neutral, unlike us.
Dialogue: 99,0:18:54.70,0:18:58.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm told not even the Green \NBerets or the SAS Air Fleet...
Dialogue: 99,0:18:58.99,0:19:02.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would be able to win if they \Nfought against the Edelweiss.
Dialogue: 99,0:19:02.33,0:19:04.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's amazing.
Dialogue: 99,0:19:04.08,0:19:09.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never expected you all to be such young, refined, and beautiful ladies.
Dialogue: 99,0:19:09.71,0:19:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You shouldn't judge women \Njust by their looks, Lt. Col.
Dialogue: 99,0:19:13.30,0:19:15.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right. Then...
Dialogue: 99,0:19:31.19,0:19:33.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did we pass the test?
Dialogue: 99,0:19:36.95,0:19:42.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like I said, you shouldn't judge women just by their looks.
Dialogue: 99,0:19:56.93,0:19:59.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alright, shall we go?
Dialogue: 99,0:20:00.26,0:20:02.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Are you sure he'll be there?
Dialogue: 99,0:20:02.76,0:20:06.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He will, if he's as big of a pervert as our information suggests.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:06.60,0:20:08.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't understand men.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:08.65,0:20:11.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The captain will guard \Nthe conference building.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:11.19,0:20:13.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The summit starts in fifteen hours.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:14.36,0:20:19.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if he's known to make \Nbombs with remote controls,
Dialogue: 99,0:20:19.49,0:20:22.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's no guarantee he's\N involved with this operation.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:22.12,0:20:28.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The captain had a few doubts about this operation when she heard about it back at HQ.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:28.79,0:20:33.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For one, the summit is taking \Nplace in a very inconvenient area.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:33.63,0:20:36.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And two, the geography \Nwould make sniping impossible.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:36.67,0:20:38.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's there to worry about, then?
Dialogue: 99,0:20:38.93,0:20:41.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Both of those things are in our favor.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:41.34,0:20:44.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It all depends on \Nyour point of view.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:44.18,0:20:46.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The remoteness makes it \Neasier to stop the enemy,
Dialogue: 99,0:20:46.39,0:20:48.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but reinforcements can't \Nget there fast, either.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:48.77,0:20:52.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if the geography makes sniping impossible, they'll depend on bombs from the start.
Dialogue: 99,0:20:52.86,0:20:56.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they're targeting the VIPs, \Nthey'd only need one bomb.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:13.08,0:21:14.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's his hobby.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:14.54,0:21:17.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No harm done, I guess, \Nbut that's not very dignified.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:18.13,0:21:22.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jean-Pierre Montan, recipient of a doctorate \Nfrom the Paris Institute of Technology.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:23.14,0:21:24.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a doctor?
Dialogue: 99,0:21:24.55,0:21:26.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why is he a Peeping Tom?
Dialogue: 99,0:21:26.06,0:21:27.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He certainly doesn't look the type.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:27.68,0:21:32.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a lot of men like that. \NWeak when it comes to booze and women.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:32.52,0:21:36.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That picture in the hall \Nwas painted by a man like that.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:36.78,0:21:39.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was it Lautrec?
Dialogue: 99,0:21:40.20,0:21:45.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least he left behind a painting, \Nbut poor Jean can't leave anything behind.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:48.41,0:21:52.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, given his proclivities,\N nobody would care if he disappeared.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:52.67,0:21:56.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he'd been with a British terrorist\N group in Interlaken two weeks ago,
Dialogue: 99,0:21:56.49,0:21:58.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,not even a dog would've noticed.
Dialogue: 99,0:21:58.30,0:22:01.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean there's a bomb inside \Nthe conference building already?
Dialogue: 99,0:22:14.94,0:22:19.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They sure picked an outrageous place to build a mountain villa.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:19.15,0:22:20.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what beautiful scenery.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:21.24,0:22:25.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Surrounded by the mountains, with a view down into the valley.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:25.16,0:22:28.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can see it all, a Tyrolian panorama, like a little miniature garden.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:28.62,0:22:31.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Alps shine, whether in the morning mist or the setting sun.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:32.54,0:22:34.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They wouldn't be able \Nto bomb this place with a plane.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:35.46,0:22:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sniping would also \Nbe geographically impossible.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:38.13,0:22:42.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's so cold here, you'd freeze to death waiting for your chance.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:42.26,0:22:45.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. Even during \Nthe day, it's -18° Celsius.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:45.34,0:22:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And at night, \Nit drops another ten degrees.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:49.01,0:22:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, let's go inside. \NThe cold is bad for our complexion.
Dialogue: 99,0:22:54.94,0:22:57.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Irene, have you finished \Nchecking the inside of the villa?
Dialogue: 99,0:22:57.94,0:23:00.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, we're almost done.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:00.11,0:23:06.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We checked every corner with magnets, \Nmetal detectors and even isotopes.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:06.62,0:23:09.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We checked the inside of the waterworks and sewage pipes, too.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:09.45,0:23:12.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good job, but please \Nbe extra careful.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:12.58,0:23:13.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:13.62,0:23:16.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, Captain, so this \Nis where you've been?
Dialogue: 99,0:23:17.42,0:23:20.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I checked ninety percent \Nof the surroundings.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:20.09,0:23:24.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's basically nothing wrong. \NNo sign of a bomb anywhere.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:25.26,0:23:28.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If an expert like Jessica says so, \Nthen it must be fine.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:30.35,0:23:31.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 99,0:23:31.39,0:23:35.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know, I just have \Na bad feeling about this.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:35.39,0:23:39.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry so much. If Jessica didn't \Nfind anything, I'm sure we're alright.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:39.65,0:23:43.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, so this is where you were?
Dialogue: 99,0:23:43.03,0:23:46.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You look like you've been busy, \Nbut I bet you haven't found anything.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:46.53,0:23:47.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We haven't.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:48.20,0:23:51.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We ripped up every floorboard when \Nwe searched this mountain villa,
Dialogue: 99,0:23:51.87,0:23:56.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and even checked the roots of every tree in a kilometer radius.
Dialogue: 99,0:23:56.16,0:24:01.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To tell the truth, we were hoping to guard \Nthe inside of the building ourselves,
Dialogue: 99,0:24:01.75,0:24:03.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but given it's a more \N"intellectual" conference,
Dialogue: 99,0:24:03.96,0:24:07.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the VIPs might find it hard to get down \Nto business with us roaming around.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:07.84,0:24:11.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, we're well aware of that.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:11.35,0:24:15.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Most of our people will be dressed \Nin maid uniforms while on guard.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:15.52,0:24:20.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Squad commanders, as well as the conference guards, will be wearing formal dresses.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:21.23,0:24:25.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, you don't seem \Nto have any weapons...
Dialogue: 99,0:24:27.20,0:24:28.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:30.12,0:24:32.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That one's on the house.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:34.91,0:24:37.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those beautiful legs are\N already deadly enough.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:38.04,0:24:40.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Though I don't think flashing\N the terrorists will help.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:40.46,0:24:44.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I really appreciate all \Nthe police and military support,
Dialogue: 99,0:24:44.55,0:24:49.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but we'll guard the conference \Nhowever we see fit.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:51.05,0:24:53.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good to hear. \NI'm leaving this up to you.
Dialogue: 99,0:24:57.31,0:24:59.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He doesn't trust us, does he?
Dialogue: 99,0:25:00.48,0:25:02.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about what he thinks.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:06.53,0:25:08.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anything from Della and Corinne?
Dialogue: 99,0:25:08.95,0:25:11.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We should get an update \Nfrom them in thirty minutes.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:14.20,0:25:17.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, are you still \Nworried about that report?
Dialogue: 99,0:25:17.54,0:25:23.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That information was just for our reference.\NIt's nothing definite, so don't worry so much.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:23.25,0:25:27.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if a British terrorist group \Ndid team up with Dr. Montan,
Dialogue: 99,0:25:27.34,0:25:31.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with security so tight, not even a mouse could get in, let alone anyone trying to set up a bomb.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:32.51,0:25:37.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They probably brought him here, decided \Nhe was useless, and then sent him home.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:37.14,0:25:41.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, he wouldn't be \Npeeping at a night club in Paris.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:42.77,0:25:47.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if they try to crash an RC helicopter \Nor a plane with a bomb on it,
Dialogue: 99,0:25:47.78,0:25:51.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it'll be detected and shot down.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:53.49,0:25:59.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'd have to get up to over 3,500 m in order to \Nclear the peak of the mountain before crashing.
Dialogue: 99,0:25:59.79,0:26:05.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unless it's a military fighter, it can't go that\N high carrying a bomb more than 500 kg,
Dialogue: 99,0:26:05.59,0:26:10.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and there'll be radio jamming from three\N directions on the day of the summit.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:10.13,0:26:12.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In short, radio is a no-go.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:14.80,0:26:19.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If there's gonna be a problem, \Nit'd be snipers from the heliport to the front,
Dialogue: 99,0:26:19.89,0:26:25.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx95}but it'd be impossible from the valley and difficult from the mountain side, given the obstructions.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:25.10,0:26:28.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jessica, what about the road from the heliport to the village front?
Dialogue: 99,0:26:28.69,0:26:30.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I checked everything.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:30.32,0:26:33.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Lt. Col. wasn't lying, they even checked the roots of the trees.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:33.95,0:26:37.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I used a detector that can pick up \Nthe sound of water running underground,
Dialogue: 99,0:26:37.53,0:26:40.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I didn't hear anything\N like a time-delay fuse.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:40.41,0:26:44.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing from my digital fuse-detecting\N pulse measuring equipment, either.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:46.29,0:26:47.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary...
Dialogue: 99,0:26:47.96,0:26:50.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll wait for Della \Nand Corinne's report.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:53.38,0:26:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure did make those things... \Nmaybe three of 'em.
Dialogue: 99,0:26:56.55,0:27:01.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was so easy. \NMere child's play.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:01.10,0:27:03.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They aren't even bombs.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:03.56,0:27:04.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not bombs?
Dialogue: 99,0:27:05.14,0:27:06.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They just make noise.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:06.65,0:27:09.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What on earth were they thinking?
Dialogue: 99,0:27:09.27,0:27:10.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just noise?
Dialogue: 99,0:27:10.44,0:27:12.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, just noise.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:12.07,0:27:16.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it sure is loud!\NLoud as the stuff they use in the strip shows.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:17.99,0:27:19.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What time did you set it for?
Dialogue: 99,0:27:19.62,0:27:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Set? I didn't set the time.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:23.09,0:27:24.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It doesn't go by time.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:25.58,0:27:27.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It goes "boom" with\N a remote control.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:27.58,0:27:34.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y'know, I could make you one that'd blow up Notre Dame, if you let me take you for a spin!
Dialogue: 99,0:27:35.05,0:27:36.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know you can.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:36.93,0:27:41.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She'll do, too! \NShe's just my type!
Dialogue: 99,0:27:45.35,0:27:49.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, where did you put \Nthese big noisemakers?
Dialogue: 99,0:27:49.48,0:27:51.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who has the remote control?
Dialogue: 99,0:27:53.28,0:27:54.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Seriously...
Dialogue: 99,0:27:55.49,0:27:57.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He won't be able to talk \Nif he keeps drinking like this.
Dialogue: 99,0:27:57.91,0:28:00.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is what it is, I guess.\N Just a bit more.
Dialogue: 99,0:28:03.58,0:28:05.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't need a remote control.
Dialogue: 99,0:28:08.08,0:28:10.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their fate is decided by the stars.
Dialogue: 99,0:28:24.02,0:28:25.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn!
Dialogue: 99,0:28:51.50,0:28:52.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not getting away!
Dialogue: 99,0:28:53.25,0:28:54.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shit.
Dialogue: 99,0:29:13.02,0:29:13.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 99,0:29:13.77,0:29:14.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 99,0:29:19.37,0:29:21.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you little—
Dialogue: 99,0:29:30.00,0:29:31.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hit 'em again!
Dialogue: 99,0:29:41.55,0:29:42.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't!
Dialogue: 99,0:29:53.56,0:29:56.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were supposed to stop them from \Nmoving, not stop them from breathing!
Dialogue: 99,0:29:56.65,0:29:58.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lost my temper...
Dialogue: 99,0:29:58.32,0:29:59.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, c'mon...
Dialogue: 99,0:29:59.74,0:30:00.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Montan is dead?!
Dialogue: 99,0:30:01.24,0:30:04.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Della's reporting from Paris, \Nget here right away!
Dialogue: 99,0:30:06.95,0:30:11.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like Dr. Peeping Tom \Nwas shot and killed by someone.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:16.63,0:30:18.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, there are bombs after all?
Dialogue: 99,0:30:18.30,0:30:19.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Should we deploy for combat?
Dialogue: 99,0:30:20.92,0:30:24.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait a second,\N it says there's three of them.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:24.43,0:30:26.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Each one has 5 grams of powder.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:26.76,0:30:27.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,5 grams?
Dialogue: 99,0:30:27.72,0:30:29.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't they mean 5 kg?
Dialogue: 99,0:30:30.18,0:30:34.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Just noise," it says. \NIt doesn't look like a mistake.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:34.44,0:30:37.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just before he was killed, \NMontan said,
Dialogue: 99,0:30:37.36,0:30:39.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Their fate is decided by the stars."
Dialogue: 99,0:30:39.82,0:30:41.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What does that mean?
Dialogue: 99,0:30:41.03,0:30:43.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Phrased like that,\N it's hard to figure anything out.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:43.36,0:30:45.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if he was a deviant, \Nhe was still a scholar.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:45.82,0:30:48.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can't believe he left \Nus with some homework.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:48.83,0:30:50.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Noise? Star?
Dialogue: 99,0:30:50.79,0:30:54.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whatever it is, it's already set up and we don't know where.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:54.87,0:30:57.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Somewhere in this mountain villa.
Dialogue: 99,0:30:57.59,0:31:01.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't we contact the Lt. Col. and get him to move the summit elsewhere?
Dialogue: 99,0:31:01.92,0:31:06.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,CAT is here to guarantee \Nthe safety of the VIPs at this summit.
Dialogue: 99,0:31:06.39,0:31:11.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And it's not the conference that's\N dangerous, it's who will be here.
Dialogue: 99,0:31:11.35,0:31:16.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx95}It'll always be high risk for the VIPs of the world to gather in one place for a confidential meeting.
Dialogue: 99,0:31:47.43,0:31:49.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Departure lobby, all is well.
Dialogue: 99,0:31:49.85,0:31:53.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Three more. \NHopefully things go smoothly.
Dialogue: 99,0:31:59.98,0:32:03.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, this is it. Check your equipment \Nand go to your assigned positions.
Dialogue: 99,0:32:06.65,0:32:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, let's go.
Dialogue: 99,0:32:08.74,0:32:09.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 99,0:32:09.99,0:32:13.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's just because the heater is on,\N but it is rather warm during the day.
Dialogue: 99,0:32:13.83,0:32:19.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right. The main dining room \Nand the guest rooms are all facing south,
Dialogue: 99,0:32:19.25,0:32:23.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the weather is especially nice today,\N which will help Jessica's group.
Dialogue: 99,0:32:54.99,0:32:57.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I need more coffee. And milk.
Dialogue: 99,0:32:57.25,0:32:58.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be ready soon.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:00.00,0:33:03.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh c'mon, I didn't think \Nwe'd be doing everything.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:04.09,0:33:06.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's about time for the carry-in \Ntruck to come for dinner.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:06.88,0:33:07.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Head to the heliport.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:08.30,0:33:11.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those kind gentlemen from \Nthe army are at the heliport,
Dialogue: 99,0:33:11.34,0:33:13.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so let those guys handle it.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:13.80,0:33:17.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter what you say, we're the only \Nones who can come in from that bridge.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:18.68,0:33:21.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sherry, Linda, Samantha, you go.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:21.23,0:33:23.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- What? \N- Us?!
Dialogue: 99,0:33:23.02,0:33:24.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No whining! Just go!
Dialogue: 99,0:33:26.53,0:33:28.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gunfights are a whole \Nlot easier than this.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:28.65,0:33:29.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're heading out!
Dialogue: 99,0:33:29.61,0:33:30.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sheesh...
Dialogue: 99,0:33:34.08,0:33:36.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whose job is it \Nto clean this section?
Dialogue: 99,0:33:40.29,0:33:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So far, so good.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:42.75,0:33:47.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, good job. Seems like \Nthings are going smoothly.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:47.46,0:33:49.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you'd expect, \Nfrom CAT's female unit.
Dialogue: 99,0:33:49.55,0:33:52.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?! These girls are \Nspecial commandos?
Dialogue: 99,0:33:52.97,0:33:54.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right. They don't \Nlook the part, do they?
Dialogue: 99,0:33:54.76,0:33:59.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought they were professional hostesses for the conference. What a surprise.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:00.60,0:34:01.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those ladies, too?
Dialogue: 99,0:34:01.77,0:34:02.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, your excellency.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:03.40,0:34:04.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come, let's go.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:04.52,0:34:06.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I'll be counting on you.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:07.86,0:34:10.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just can't see them as anything but ordinary middle-aged guys.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:10.65,0:34:14.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, but the decisions \Nthey make change the world.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:14.49,0:34:19.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, there's still time before dinner,\N let's go help with the preparation, too.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:26.46,0:34:31.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The temperature goes up... surrounded by the mountains in three directions... all facing south.
Dialogue: 99,0:34:32.05,0:34:35.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Noise, loud noise... three of them...
Dialogue: 99,0:34:35.39,0:34:36.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, what's wrong?
Dialogue: 99,0:34:37.47,0:34:40.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Three bombs... on the slopes...
Dialogue: 99,0:34:42.10,0:34:43.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary?
Dialogue: 99,0:34:46.77,0:34:48.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, what's wrong?!
Dialogue: 99,0:34:48.48,0:34:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Call Lt. Col. Heineken!
Dialogue: 99,0:34:50.23,0:34:53.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Helga, the leaders! \NEvacuate the VIPs!
Dialogue: 99,0:34:53.53,0:34:54.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary...
Dialogue: 99,0:34:54.28,0:34:55.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't have time! Hurry!
Dialogue: 99,0:34:55.99,0:34:58.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, calm down... what is it?
Dialogue: 99,0:34:58.45,0:35:02.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An avalanche! The terrorists are gonna \Ncrush the whole villa in an avalanche!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:02.66,0:35:03.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:03.87,0:35:06.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is Heineken, \Nwhat's wrong, Captain Mary?
Dialogue: 99,0:35:06.71,0:35:10.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col., recall your soldiers out on \Nthose three mountains immediately!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:10.50,0:35:12.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 99,0:35:12.59,0:35:15.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have there been any \Nmountain-climbing parties recently?
Dialogue: 99,0:35:15.58,0:35:21.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, about eight parties climbed this month, \Nbut the last one descended two weeks ago.
Dialogue: 99,0:35:21.81,0:35:23.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So there should be \Nno problem with—
Dialogue: 99,0:35:23.18,0:35:25.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bombs are set \Non those mountains!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:25.56,0:35:26.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:28.02,0:35:29.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you certain?!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:29.73,0:35:31.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Seems like dinner\N has been carried in.
Dialogue: 99,0:35:31.44,0:35:32.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 99,0:35:33.99,0:35:35.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, who are those two?
Dialogue: 99,0:35:35.40,0:35:36.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col.! What's wrong?!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:39.33,0:35:41.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are they also members of CAT?
Dialogue: 99,0:35:41.74,0:35:44.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col.! Lt. Col. Heineken! \NWhat's wrong?!
Dialogue: 99,0:35:44.91,0:35:49.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx95}Excuse me, Captain Helga, but the President's aide would like to make contact with Washington,
Dialogue: 99,0:35:49.96,0:35:52.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so he wants to use \Nthe comms satellite.
Dialogue: 99,0:35:52.30,0:35:53.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, sure.
Dialogue: 99,0:35:53.80,0:35:55.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Comms satellite?
Dialogue: 99,0:35:57.22,0:35:59.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Their fate is decided by the stars."
Dialogue: 99,0:35:59.01,0:35:59.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The stars?
Dialogue: 99,0:36:00.20,0:36:00.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Transmission!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:01.85,0:36:02.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't! Helga!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:07.40,0:36:09.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What's going on?
Dialogue: 99,0:36:30.04,0:36:31.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, the bridge!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:31.59,0:36:32.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col.!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:33.34,0:36:35.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We still have time before \Nthe avalanche reaches the villa!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:35.71,0:36:37.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get the VIPs out of there!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:37.43,0:36:38.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:36:48.77,0:36:50.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col., w-we can't get across!
Dialogue: 99,0:37:01.78,0:37:03.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Evacuate! Evacuate!
Dialogue: 99,0:37:10.75,0:37:12.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone, remain calm.
Dialogue: 99,0:37:12.79,0:37:13.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary...
Dialogue: 99,0:37:16.38,0:37:18.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jessica, open Container E!
Dialogue: 99,0:37:22.64,0:37:25.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are parachutes that will quickly fill with helium gas.
Dialogue: 99,0:37:26.22,0:37:28.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They inflate in 0.3 seconds,
Dialogue: 99,0:37:28.64,0:37:34.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and can carry 80 kg descending at \N0.8 m/second, using an electronic sensor.
Dialogue: 99,0:37:41.41,0:37:43.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Avalanche approaching!\N1,000 meters away!
Dialogue: 99,0:37:44.53,0:37:47.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please jump off from \Nthe south cliff with these.
Dialogue: 99,0:37:49.25,0:37:52.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The wind is blowing towards the valley, \Nso you'll be able to land in the village below.
Dialogue: 99,0:37:52.92,0:37:54.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,W-We can't do that!
Dialogue: 99,0:37:54.63,0:37:56.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry! Do you want to die?!
Dialogue: 99,0:37:56.42,0:37:57.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's coming!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:08.43,0:38:09.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone, hurry up!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:20.82,0:38:23.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry up, get out of here.
Dialogue: 99,0:38:23.28,0:38:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, Captain, there aren't enough parachutes for your group!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:26.28,0:38:27.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forget about us, just go!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:27.97,0:38:28.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And hurry!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:32.79,0:38:34.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that all of them?
Dialogue: 99,0:38:34.25,0:38:37.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, some of them are still inside!\NCaptain Mary's still there!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:46.81,0:38:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The mountain villa!
Dialogue: 99,0:38:57.27,0:38:59.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, the pipes have been set up.
Dialogue: 99,0:39:03.61,0:39:05.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry! The villa foundation \Nis falling apart!
Dialogue: 99,0:39:13.91,0:39:15.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col., t-the villa...
Dialogue: 99,0:39:17.59,0:39:18.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Captain!\N- Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:39:19.67,0:39:20.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 99,0:39:44.19,0:39:45.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col.!
Dialogue: 99,0:39:55.54,0:39:57.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Captain Mary!
Dialogue: 99,0:39:57.75,0:39:58.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:40:05.63,0:40:07.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a close call.
Dialogue: 99,0:40:07.55,0:40:13.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah, but isn't there something we can do about our outfits?
Dialogue: 99,0:40:13.47,0:40:17.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't have much time to change in a rush job like that.
Dialogue: 99,0:40:17.02,0:40:20.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, this is the finale, \Nso why not give them a show?
Dialogue: 99,0:40:31.20,0:40:33.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Captain!\N- Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:40:36.62,0:40:38.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you all alright?
Dialogue: 99,0:40:39.87,0:40:41.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness you're safe!
Dialogue: 99,0:40:42.28,0:40:44.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col., what about the VIPs?
Dialogue: 99,0:40:45.34,0:40:48.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All safe. They'll continue the summit in another conference building.
Dialogue: 99,0:40:48.76,0:40:50.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Politicians sure are tough, huh?
Dialogue: 99,0:40:51.93,0:40:54.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, here's a message \Nfrom all of them.
Dialogue: 99,0:40:56.48,0:41:02.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"The terrorists' evil plot was foiled by the goddesses sent to protect us."
Dialogue: 99,0:41:02.82,0:41:07.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"We thank you all. \NGlory to you, brave Valkyries."
Dialogue: 99,0:41:11.91,0:41:13.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I've learned a lot.
Dialogue: 99,0:41:13.78,0:41:17.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You shouldn't judge women \Njust by their looks, for one.
Dialogue: 99,0:41:20.33,0:41:23.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Operation completed, 15:30.
Dialogue: 99,0:41:23.00,0:41:24.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, withdraw!
Dialogue: 99,0:41:41.44,0:41:43.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are we going \Nto do with that girl?
Dialogue: 99,0:41:43.56,0:41:45.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, Helga,\N you're getting your fair share of attention.
Dialogue: 99,0:41:46.90,0:41:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 99,0:41:48.94,0:41:50.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I'm too old for that, now.
Dialogue: 99,0:41:51.17,0:41:53.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're at the peak of our womanhood.
Dialogue: 99,0:41:57.41,0:41:57.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 99,0:41:57.95,0:42:00.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mary, sorry to disturb you \Nwhile you're on vacation,
Dialogue: 99,0:42:00.63,0:42:02.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but could you \Ncome to Matagora—
Dialogue: 99,0:42:06.30,0:42:09.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was it okay to do that? \NWasn't that the Colonel?
Dialogue: 99,0:42:09.05,0:42:14.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course it was. \NEven brave goddesses need a vacation.
Dialogue: 99,0:42:14.01,0:42:14.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:42:14.82,0:42:16.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,- Captain!\N- Captain!
Dialogue: 99,0:42:40.58,0:42:48.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look back across \Nhundreds of millions of years.
Dialogue: 99,0:42:49.76,0:42:57.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You should be able to\N understand the power of life.
Dialogue: 99,0:42:58.89,0:43:02.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The fish are at \Nthe bottom of the sea,
Dialogue: 99,0:43:03.48,0:43:08.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,while we are beneath the Sun,
Dialogue: 99,0:43:08.02,0:43:15.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and for thousands of years \Nwe have struggled on!
Dialogue: 99,0:43:16.91,0:43:19.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Under the stars!
Dialogue: 99,0:43:21.28,0:43:23.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Born under the stars!
Dialogue: 99,0:43:25.75,0:43:35.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Run beyond time, all the way to the ends of eternity.
Dialogue: 99,0:43:44.52,0:43:48.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you want to be reborn anew,
Dialogue: 99,0:43:49.11,0:43:53.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if you want to feel your true self,
Dialogue: 99,0:43:53.90,0:44:01.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then unravel the myths of the Incas.
Dialogue: 99,0:44:02.91,0:44:11.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Painful memories are just dreams before awakening.
Dialogue: 99,0:44:12.09,0:44:19.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The shining stars are always on our side.
Dialogue: 99,0:44:21.01,0:44:23.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Under the stars!
Dialogue: 99,0:44:25.27,0:44:27.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Born under the stars!
Dialogue: 99,0:44:29.81,0:44:38.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Run beyond time, all the way to the ends of eternity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.45,0:00:15.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,
